":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-05-29T08:41:48Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T09:54:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.6.3.stable and 4.7.beta3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta3 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13500 (20 threads) - 31.78 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen adding children to a `HFlowContainer` that is in a `ScrollContainer`, the scrollbar appears from the moment it can no longer show all of the elements. But when removing, the scrollbar does not disappear as soon as it can show all of the elements.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4bafa22e-b280-47cc-826d-40146e2ebb95\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Have a `HFlowContainer` inside a `ScrollContainer`\n2. Add children until scrollbar appears\n3. Remove child\n4. Scrollbar should disappear, but it does not\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[scroll-hflow_mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28383265/scroll-hflow_mrp.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119864/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119864/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}